Subject: Enable the upstream cargo test suite in debian/rules
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Uncomment override_dh_auto_test so dh_auto_test runs cargo test --all.
Base-Tree: debian rust-fd-find 10.2.0-1
Verify: cmd `dhi def build --fast --platform linux/amd64 package/deb/main/rust-fd-find/debian-13/10.yaml` expect "test result: ok. 102 passed; 0 failed"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI producer test requirement; upstream tests are not disabled)
Drop-When: never: retire when a Debian rust-fd-find source's debian/rules enables override_dh_auto_test itself (sid 10.5.0-1 still comments it out)

Debian's debian/rules for rust-fd-find 10.2.0-1 comments out override_dh_auto_test with the note "Disable
because the test still using tempdir (instead of tempfile)". That note does not hold for this source: the
upstream tests/testenv/mod.rs imports tempfile::TempDir and creates its fixtures with
tempfile::Builder::tempdir(). Without this override dh_auto_test runs only cargo build, so the upstream suite
never executes. The test dev-dependencies (diff, filetime, tempfile, test-case) are added to contents.builds in
the definition so cargo test resolves them offline.

--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -13,6 +13,5 @@
 	# Don't do anything. fails because of the
 	# https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/66118
 
-# Disable because the test still using tempdir (instead of tempfile)
-# override_dh_auto_test:
-# 	dh_auto_test -- test --all
+override_dh_auto_test:
+	dh_auto_test -- test --all
